- op: create  # ff3f
  at: '2026-09-26T23:42:15Z'  # ff3f
  by: agent  # ff3f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ff3f
  clock: 1  # ff3f
  nonce: ff3f  # ff3f
  data:  # ff3f
    kind: work_item  # ff3f
    title: "swift emits no symbol for an initializer (init / convenience init), so init bodies' calls anchor on the type and a constructor call cannot land on the init"  # ff3f
    status: todo_hard  # ff3f
    priority: 3  # ff3f
    parent:  # ff3f
    tags:  # ff3f
    - swift  # ff3f
    - analysis_quality  # ff3f
    - call_graph  # ff3f
    isbefore: []  # ff3f
    duplicate_of: []  # ff3f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ff3f
    pr_ref:  # ff3f
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-26 in INV-bamij's swift read-back (hummingbird). The swift analyzer emits NO symbol for an initializer (`init(...)` / `convenience init` / `required init`): TrieRouter.swift's RouterPathTrieBuilder has symbols for the struct and its methods (addEntry, build, ...) but none for its `init()`. Before INV-bamij's second batch a call inside an init therefore emitted no edge at all; since then it is anchored on the enclosing type (hummingbird: 162 new edges on structs, many of them init bodies such as `self.root = Node(key: .null, output: nil)` and `self.idleTimer = idleTimeout.map { ... }`).\n\nWHAT IS LOST: the init as a node. A slice or a dead-code query cannot name `RouterPathTrieBuilder.init`, a call INTO an init (a constructor call `RouterPathTrieBuilder()`) cannot land on it, and the init's calls are attributed to the type rather than to the initializer that makes them.\n\nNOT CHECKED: deinit, subscript declarations and computed-property accessors, which are the same family of \"callable member with no symbol\" in swift; nor how many inits a typical repository has."  # ff3f
    fields: {}  # ff3f
- op: discuss  # 5453
  at: '2026-10-04T10:36:03Z'  # 5453
  by: agent  # 5453
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5453
  clock: 2  # 5453
  nonce: '5453'  # 5453
  message: "BEARS ON THIS ITEM (found 2026-10-04 while working WI-binap, the C# half of the same \"declaration kind missing from the enclosing set\" family). Reproduced on analyze_swift (base 2a98abb55d):\n\n    class A {\n        var watched: Int = 0 {\n            didSet { _ = helper() }      // line 8\n        }\n        deinit { _ = helper2() }         // line 11\n        ...\n    }\n    calls: A(class) -> A.helper  line 8    (willSet/didSet observer: A.watched exists as kind=field and spans the observer, but is not in the callable set)\n           A(class) -> A.helper2 line 11   (deinit: no symbol, as init has none)\n\nComputed properties, get/set accessors and subscripts are already credited correctly (A.twice / A.full / A.subscript(i:)). So the swift residual of this family is: init (this item), deinit, and property observers. Not measured on a corpus."  # 5453
- op: discuss  # 135a
  at: '2026-10-20T23:40:26Z'  # 135a
  by: agent  # 135a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 135a
  clock: 3  # 135a
  nonce: 135a  # 135a
  message: "Status check 2026-10-20: still open on dev 2760e4010b. On a fixture with struct Builder { init() { self.root = helper() }; deinit { cleanup() } }, hypergumbo run emits no init or deinit symbol, and the helper()/cleanup() calls are anchored on Builder:struct. (swift.py's _SWIFT_SCOPE_NODES lists init_declaration/deinit_declaration for receiver typing only.) Unmerged work: worktree ~/hg_wt/sogof, local branch jgstern-agent/fix/sogof, own commits b02b95091d (init/deinit symbols) and 17c23c0c37 (module_key_axis pins), on base c6b299a052. Cherry-pick only those two onto origin/dev. Recompute the swift.py module_key_axis pins by anchor, because 17c23c0c37's numbers predate later swift.py edits, and run test_module_key_axis explicitly. Last run on the branch: 43 targeted tests, no coverage verdict."  # 135a
