- op: discuss  # be31
  at: '2026-10-22T01:58:10Z'  # be31
  by: agent  # be31
  actor: jgstern_agent  # be31
  clock: 5  # be31
  nonce: be31  # be31
  message: "Fixed in PR #1796 (dev e3ea9db6c9). Cherry-picked b02b95091d onto dev and ported its init chooser to ADR-0039 ruling 6 (an ambiguous choice passes resolution_score = match quality x 1/sqrt(N), not a precomputed confidence); module_key_axis swift pins re-anchored (2604 -> 3056, 2533 -> 2979); some/any/P&Q parameter types are read so a trailing closure never binds them. Repro on merged dev ('hypergumbo run' on struct Builder { init() { self.root = helper() } }, class Holder { deinit { cleanup() } }, func make() { _ = Builder() }): exit 0; nodes constructor Builder.init and method Holder.deinit; calls Builder.init -> helper (line 5), Holder.deinit -> cleanup (line 8), make -> Builder.init (line 10). Before: no init/deinit node, both calls anchored on Builder:struct / Holder:class. Census (vapor, Kingfisher, Alamofire, hummingbird, TCA, SwiftLint): calls counts identical; 1253 init + 25 deinit symbols; 13417 calls land on an init. RESIDUAL: the chooser does not model access control -- TCA's 458 'Reduce { }' calls are ambiguous between init(internal:) and init(_:), and the first-by-position pick is the internal one, invisible outside the module. NOT CHECKED (as filed): subscripts/accessors were already credited; nothing else re-measured."  # be31
